-- title:
--   Equal kernels: Hecke algebras on S₂(Γ₀(p)) and on J₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a nonzero natural number and suppose that the Hecke operators on the Jacobian commute, i.e. `HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar p` holds: for all primes $\ell,\ell'$ the $\mathbb Z$-linear endomorphisms `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ` and `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ'` of `JZero p` commute, where `JZero p` is the degree-zero divisor class group of the modular function field of level $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (taken as `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) and `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ` is the endomorphism induced by `heckeOperatorAlong` over that algebraic closure. Two ring homomorphisms out of the abstract Hecke algebra `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb Z[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ are compared. The first is `heckeEvalForms p 2`, sending $X_\ell$ to $U_\ell$ if $\ell \mid p$ and to $T_\ell$ otherwise inside the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra `heckeAlgebra p 2 ∅` of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(p)))$ generated by those operators, followed by `latticeRestrictHom p ∅`, which restricts such an operator to the integral lattice `intLattice p 2` and records it in the image algebra `heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅`. The second is `heckeEvalBar h`, sending $X_\ell$ to `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ` in $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb Z}(\mathrm{JZero}\ p)$, formed through the commutative subalgebra generated by the range of `heckeOperatorBar`. The assertion is that these two ring homomorphisms have the same kernel.
--
--   This is the standard identification of the Hecke algebra acting on weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(p)$ with the Hecke algebra acting on $J_0(p)$, stated at the level of kernels so that ring-theoretic information transports between the forms side and the Jacobian side; the Jacobian is taken over an algebraically closed field. It is used in the construction of Hecke-stable lattices in Tate modules, in the analysis of idempotents attached to the Eisenstein part of the torsion, and in divisibility statements for lattice-restricted Hecke operators annihilating the Jacobian.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ker_heckeEvalForms_latticeRestrict_eq_ker_heckeEvalBar.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeLocal
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeEvalForms
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_HeckeModule

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open ModularCurve CuspForm

theorem ModularCurve.ker_heckeEvalForms_latticeRestrict_eq_ker_heckeEvalBar
    (p : ℕ) [NeZero p] (h : HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar p) :
    RingHom.ker ((latticeRestrictHom p ∅).toRingHom.comp (heckeEvalForms p 2)) =
      RingHom.ker (heckeEvalBar h) := by sorry
